World "Closure"
Title "Closure Properties"

Introduction "
Which operations on languages keep them **regular**, recognisable by a DFA?

In this world you'll build new machines out of old ones. You'll flip a
machine's verdict, and you'll run two machines side by side. Then you'll prove
that regular languages are closed under complement, intersection and union.
"
